/**
@page cosmology_tools Source and workflow catalog

Every maintained simulation/reference source and Python/shell workflow is listed below.
Generated result trees, the paper source and downloaded upstream dependency trees are evidence or external inputs, not part of this API extraction.
Commands run from the repository root. `python` denotes the configured OPALX environment (`/Users/adelmann/.venv-h6/bin/python` locally).
Uppercase values are placeholders; use the tool-specific usage/help to select actual fresh paths and native executables.
CLI guard bodies are source-browser material, not importable APIs; this does not exclude the functions they call.

@section tools_binaries Compiled programs and shared model
| File | Purpose | Entry point/contract |
|---|---|---|
| @ref Cosmology.cpp | Main generated-IC evolution | `Cosmology input.par` or `Cosmology --self-test` |
| @ref CosmologyConfig.h | Validated parameter object | @ref cosmology::Config |
| @ref CosmologyPhysics.h | Host growth/spectrum/quadrature | @ref cosmology::Background and @ref cosmology::PowerSpectrum |
| @ref CosmologySimulation.h | Distributed CIC/FFT/KDK state | @ref cosmology::Simulation |
| @ref ExecutionMetadata.h | Host/device execution reporting | @ref cosmology::writeExecutionMetadata |
| @ref CompareCosmologyForce.cpp | Shared frozen-force import | `CompareCosmologyForce N L Omega_m input.csv output_dir` |
| @ref CompareCosmologyEvolution.cpp | Shared synchronized phase-space evolution | `CompareCosmologyEvolution NP NM L Omega_m ai af steps checkpoints input.csv output_dir` |
| @ref TestCosmologyPhysics.cpp | Host numerical/regression sanity | `TestCosmologyPhysics` (no MPI launcher required) |
| @ref FastPMForce.c | Native pinned force harness | `FastPMForce N L Omega_m input.csv output_dir` |
| @ref FastPMEvolution.c | Native ordinary plain-PM harness | `FastPMEvolution NP NM L Omega_m ai af steps checkpoints input.csv output_dir` |
| @ref CompareZarijaPhysics.cpp | Original-initializer public-model probe | `CompareZarijaPhysics input.par output.csv` |
| @ref ReferenceABI.cpp | Original-initializer ABI sizes/endian probe | Built and run by the Zarija reference builder |

All native applications preserve their stated model/precision assumptions. Import adapters are diagnostics, not a distributed checkpoint API. See @ref cosmology_contracts and @ref cosmology_references.

@section tools_python Python programs and helper modules

@subsection tool_python_analyze_zeldovich_benchmark_py python/analyze_zeldovich_benchmark.py
@ref analyze_zeldovich_benchmark.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Audit saved broadband IPPL/FastPM snapshots and compute CIC power spectra.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
python -B demos/cosmology/python/analyze_zeldovich_benchmark.py
@endcode

@subsection tool_python_compare_fixture_files_py python/compare_fixture_files.py
@ref compare_fixture_files.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Read-only cross-host comparison of common-particle cosmology fixture CSVs.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
python -B demos/cosmology/python/compare_fixture_files.py ORIGINAL COMPARISON --box-size BOX_SIZE --output OUTPUT
@endcode

@subsection tool_python_gadget2_analyze_gadget2_np256_py python/gadget2/analyze_gadget2_np256.py
@ref analyze_gadget2_np256.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Verify a completed matched Gadget-2 256^3 run and measure its z=0 spectrum.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
python -B demos/cosmology/python/gadget2/analyze_gadget2_np256.py
@endcode
This is the historical fixed Merlin 256³ workflow; its host/root/hash restrictions remain intact. The portable local 128³ workflow is run_three_code_campaign.py, not a silent retargeting of these records.

@subsection tool_python_gadget2_convert_shared_ic_py python/gadget2/convert_shared_ic.py
@ref convert_shared_ic.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Convert the frozen shared cosmology CSV IC to GADGET-2 format-1.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
python -B demos/cosmology/python/gadget2/convert_shared_ic.py --input INPUT --output OUTPUT --redshift REDSHIFT --expected-sha256 EXPECTED_SHA256
@endcode

@subsection tool_python_gadget2_plot_three_code_np256_py python/gadget2/plot_three_code_np256.py
@ref plot_three_code_np256.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Plot matched 256^3-particle IPPL, FastPM, and GADGET-2 z=0 spectra.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
python -B demos/cosmology/python/gadget2/plot_three_code_np256.py
@endcode
This is the historical fixed Merlin 256³ workflow; its host/root/hash restrictions remain intact. The portable local 128³ workflow is run_three_code_campaign.py, not a silent retargeting of these records.

@subsection tool_python_gadget2_run_gadget2_np256_py python/gadget2/run_gadget2_np256.py
@ref run_gadget2_np256.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Run an audited GADGET-2 TreePM 256^3-particle/mesh comparison on Merlin.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
python -B demos/cosmology/python/gadget2/run_gadget2_np256.py
@endcode
This is the historical fixed Merlin 256³ workflow; its host/root/hash restrictions remain intact. The portable local 128³ workflow is run_three_code_campaign.py, not a silent retargeting of these records.

@subsection tool_python_gaussian_fixture_py python/gaussian_fixture.py
@ref gaussian_fixture.py "Source/API reference".

**Purpose.** Common-particle, band-limited Gaussian 1LPT fixtures for local PM studies.

**Usage.**
@code{.sh}
PYTHONPATH=demos/cosmology/python python -c "import gaussian_fixture"
@endcode
This is an importable host helper, not a standalone simulation driver. Its function-level contracts define array shapes, units and returned records.

